  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry the fresh produce.",
      "secondary_message": "2 leeks\n4 medium carrots\n4 sticks celery"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Drain and rinse the beans in a colander; set aside to drain further.",
      "secondary_message": "2 (266 g) cans cannellini (white kidney) beans"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Trim off root end and dark green top of the leeks, leaving only the white and pale green parts. Cut leeks in half lengthwise and rinse under running water, separating the layers to remove any dirt and grit. Slice crosswise into ¼-inch thick pieces and place in a medium bowl. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel, trim, and small dice carrots. Add to the bowl with the leek. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Trim and thinly slice celery crosswise. Add to the bowl. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a large ovenproof skillet over medium-high heat. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "While the skillet heats up, peel and mince garlic. Add to the bowl with the veggies. ",
      "secondary_message": "2 cloves garlic"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add veggies, garlic, and spices; cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, 4-5 minutes. (Reserve bowl for later use.)",
      "secondary_message": "4 tsp extra virgin olive oil\n1 tsp paprika\n1 tsp salt\n½ tsp black pepper\n½ tsp thyme, dried"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, preheat oven to broil on high and position rack in the upper third of the oven.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Coarsely grate cheese. Place in the reserved bowl and set aside. ",
      "secondary_message": "⅔ (227 g) block mozzarella cheese"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the veggies are softened, add beans, tomato sauce, water, and Worcestershire to the skillet; stir to combine and bring to a simmer. Once simmering, reduce heat to low and continue to cook, stirring occasionally, until sauce is slightly thickened, 3-4 minutes more. ",
      "secondary_message": "2 (221 g) cans tomato sauce\n2 tsp Worcestershire sauce"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "While the beans are cooking, chop or tear prosciutto into bite-sized pieces. ",
      "secondary_message": "8 slices prosciutto"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the sauce is slightly thickened, top skillet with cheese and prosciutto. Place in the oven and broil until cheese is melted and prosciutto is crispy, 3-4 minutes. Remove from oven.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the skillet is done, arrange bread on a large baking sheet pan. Place in the oven and broil, flipping halfway through, until lightly toasted, 1-2 minutes. Remove from oven and cut in half. (Alternatively, you can use a toaster.)",
      "secondary_message": "8 slices whole grain bread"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide cheesy bean skillet and toast between plates or bowls. Enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
